A developer implements the following code to sort a singly linked list using bubble sort by swapping data instead of links:
void sort(struct Node *head) {
struct Node *i, *j;
int temp;
for (i = head; i != NULL; i = i->next) {
for (j = i->next; j != NULL; j = j->next) {
if (i->data > j->data) {
temp = i->data;
i->data = j->data;
j->data = temp;
}
}
}
}
After sorting, the program prints the list, but the last element sometimes remains unsorted when the list contains duplicate values. What is the most likely conceptual issue?

